//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Delete Head of Circular Linked List

Given a circular linked list, delete the head node and
return the last node of the modified list.

Notes
- If list is empty or has only one node, return null.
- After deletion the last node must point to the new head.

Constraints
1  ≤  number of nodes  ≤  10⁵
0  ≤  node.data        ≤  10⁵

Sample Input 1
  head → 1 → 7 → 8 → 10 → (back to 1)

Sample Output 1
  7 → 8 → 10 → (back to 7)

  BEFORE                              AFTER
  head                                      curr
   │                                         │
   ▼                                         ▼
 [1|.]──►[7|.]──►[8|.]──►[10|.]     [7|.]──►[8|.]──►[10|.]
   ▲                          │        ▲                  │
   └──────────────────────────┘        └──────────────────┘


Sample Input 2
  head → 3 → 9 → (back to 3)

Sample Output 2
  9 → (back to 9)

  BEFORE                    AFTER
  head                       curr
   │                          │
   ▼                          ▼
 [3|.]──►[9|.]      [9|.]──►[9|.]
   ▲          │       ▲          │
   └──────────┘       └──────────┘


Sample Input 3
  head → 5 → (back to 5)   (single node)

Sample Output 3
  null  ✅
